# Lab 03 – Building Your First PLC Program

## Overview

This lab focuses on developing and validating a basic PLC control program using **OpenPLC Editor** and **Ladder Diagram (LD)** programming.

The project implements an automated tank-filling control system with level monitoring, alarms, an emergency stop, and automatic valve control.

## Objectives

- Create a PLC project using OpenPLC Editor.
- Define BOOL and REAL PLC variables.
- Implement automatic tank filling logic.
- Implement high-level and low-level alarms.
- Implement emergency-stop functionality.
- Compile and run the PLC program in simulation.
- Validate the control logic using the OpenPLC debugger.

## Tank Control Logic

The system uses the following setpoints:

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---:|
| Tank Empty Setpoint | 2.0 ft |
| Tank Full Setpoint | 8.0 ft |
| Low-Level Alarm Setpoint | 1.0 ft |
| High-Level Alarm Setpoint | 9.0 ft |

The filling valve is commanded open when automatic filling is active and the high-level alarm is not active.

Automatic filling starts when the tank level is at or below the empty setpoint and stops when the full setpoint, high-level alarm, or emergency stop condition is reached.

## Main Variables

- `TankFillAuto_Cmd` – Automatic filling command
- `TankValveOpen` – Tank valve command
- `Estop_Cmd` – Emergency stop command
- `TankLevelHi_Alarm` – High-level alarm
- `TankLevelLo_Alarm` – Low-level alarm
- `TankLevel_LIT` – Tank level measurement
- `TankEmpty_SP` – Empty level setpoint
- `TankFull_SP` – Full level setpoint
- `TankLoAlarm_SP` – Low-level alarm setpoint
- `TankHiAlarm_SP` – High-level alarm setpoint

## Tools

- OpenPLC Editor
- Ladder Diagram (LD)
- OpenPLC Runtime/Simulation
- PLC Debugger

## Validation

The program was successfully compiled and transferred to the OpenPLC simulation environment. Runtime variables were monitored using the debugger to verify the tank-filling control logic and alarm states.

## Evidence

This folder contains the PLC project files, program screenshots, and supporting documentation for the lab.

